  data: {
    LLM: "1. Turn: On your turn, you draw one card (from the Stock or the Discard Pile) and then discard one card face-up.\n2. One-Card Limit: You must always have exactly 4 cards at the end of your turn.\n3. The Stop: Any player who has four cards of the SAME SUIT can declare 'Stop' (Selesai). The hand ends immediately.",
    Player: "1. Turn: On your turn, you draw one card (from the Stock or the Discard Pile) and then discard one card face-up.\n2. One-Card Limit: You must always have exactly 4 cards at the end of your turn.\n3. The Stop: Any player who has four cards of the SAME SUIT can declare 'Stop' (Selesai). The hand ends immediately.",
    objective: 'Collect four cards of the same suit to maximize your score (maximum 41).',
    gameplay: "1. Turn: On your turn, you draw one card (from the Stock or the Discard Pile) and then discard one card face-up.\n2. One-Card Limit: You must always have exactly 4 cards at the end of your turn.\n3. The Stop: Any player who has four cards of the SAME SUIT can declare 'Stop' (Selesai). The hand ends immediately.",
    keyRules: [
      "You cannot pick up the previous player's discard and immediately discard it back.",
      'If the Stock runs out, the discard pile is shuffled to form a new Stock.',
      "If a player 'Stops' and their 4-card suit sum is lower than an opponent's mixed-hand sum, the stopper still wins the round in some house rules, but usually, the highest score wins regardless.",
